  "title": "Chapter 33: Atmosphere",
  "order": 34,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qwc7ns6",
      "content": "The atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding the Earth. It is essential for life because it provides oxygen for breathing, carbon dioxide for photosynthesis, and protects the Earth from harmful solar radiation. The atmosphere also regulates temperature and weather patterns."
    },
    {
